:0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":5,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I'm approving PKT-0073. The investigation does what the goal asked, the data backs it up, and no file was changed during review.\n\n**Goal and evidence**\n- **Self time:** the packet asked to attribute the ~300 ms drawings self time on pptx open by function, or state that no function exceeds 50 ms. The baseline gives a per-function table showing the largest single function takes about 31 ms. That answers the \"none exceeds 50 ms\" branch.\n- **Refactor candidate:** a candidate with an expected gain is still named: per-shape text styles, `recalculateTextStyles`, at 143 ms including its callees.\n- **Raw data:** the JSON matches the figures quoted. `CShape.Get_Styles` is 144.1 ms inclusive, `recalculateTextStyles` 143.3 ms, and `CMemory.sha256` 6.1 ms self and 91 ms inclusive.\n- **Comparison opens:** docx and xlsx were measured as asked.\n- **sdkjs-slide coordination:** this is thin, but it is stated openly. The baseline and the spawn request name the slide-side callers: `SlideLayout.recalculate`, `Slide.recalculateSpTree` and `MasterSlide.recalculate`.\n\n**Contract, scope and budget**\n- **Files:** only `baseline.md` was edited, and the new files are under `.theseus/oracle/perf`. The `.theseus/spawn/` request and the friction line are the method's own bookkeeping, not code changes.\n- **Size:** 671 lines across 6 files, within the 800-line, 6-file budget.\n- **Tests:** none were touched.\n- **New script:** `drawings-functions.js` runs the helper part of `profile-client.js` (everything before its `main()`) rather than copying it. That is brittle if that file changes later, but acceptable for an oracle tool.\n\n**TEP-0004 checks**\n- **Executor log:** it is filled in.\n- **Follow-up request:** it exists in `.theseus/spawn/`, with `requires: [documentserver, browser]` and a contract that keeps resolved text styles identical. It also notes it needs the sdkjs fork, which is correct because `external/sdkjs` is a read-only clone.\n- **Surprises:** both are recorded in the baseline. One is font loading being counted as drawings; the other is file names sometimes being wrong. The characterize-packet rule doesn't apply, because this is an investigate packet.\n\n**Minor points (not blocking)**\n- **Shared sha256 cost:** `CMemory.sha256` also costs about 93 ms inclusive on one of the docx samples, about the same as on pptx. That points to a word style-cache cost shared across editors, not one specific to pptx shapes. The refactor packet should take it into account, and its gain estimate may be optimistic for the shape-level cache alone.\n- **No rerun command:** the packet has no acceptance commands, so nothing can rerun this result automatically. Reproducing it means running the script by hand.\n\nVERDICT: APPROVE Per-function breakdown matches raw data, answers the goal (no function over 50 ms self; style-building candidate requested as a refactor)","ttft_ms":2493,"type":"result","duration_ms":22772,"uuid":"7d2c3445-7e13-4e69-9718-29e590f77abd","ttft_stream_ms":962,"time_to_request_ms":276,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":10,"system_prompt":40,"resume_other":1,"process_user_input":9,"input_attachments":40,"input_hooks":4,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":80,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":4,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":12,"query_setup":4,"auto_mode_context_wait":11,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":26,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":11,"request_build":8},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":125,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":208,"time_to_request_major_faults":1,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":213,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":138,"process_rss_mib_result":223,"process_anon_mib_result":135,"process_peak_rss_mib":234,"process_cpu_ms_turn":949,"process_wall_ms_turn":22771,"process_